                <pb facs="0192" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1930v02/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">893.00/10769: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Johnson</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-03-16T15:00:00+08:00">March 16, 1930—3
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received March 16—6:15 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>198. Following from American Consul General at Hankow: <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“March 15, noon. Steamship <hi rendition="#italic">Chi Ping</hi> of
                            Yangtze Rapid Company with armed naval guard aboard was heavily fired on
                            at mileage 46 to 48 above Ichang yesterday and Lieutenant C. M. Winslow,
                            officer in charge of armed guard, slightly wounded and five Chinese
                            wounded. <hi rendition="#italic">Chi Ping</hi> was hit about 300 times
                            by rifle bullets and three shells fired at the vessel from field pieces
                            but no hits. Other vessels of Yangtze Rapid Company are being escorted
                            today through the danger zone by the U. S. S. <hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Tutuila</hi>. Steamship <hi rendition="#italic">I’Ping</hi> also
                            attacked same place and same day, one Chinese passenger killed. Armed
                            guard returned fire both cases with rifle fire and machine guns,
                            casualties observed among soldiers ashore who directed the fire against
                            the American vessels with rifles, machine guns, and field pieces.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer>For the Minister:<lb/><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                        >Perkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
